G0166.def:
**αἰώνιος**, -ον (as usual in Attic), also -α, -ον. [[2Th.2.16|2Th.2:16]], [[Heb.9.12|Heb.9:12]];
(αἰών), [in LXX chiefly for עוֹלָם ;]
**age-long, eternal**,
(a) **of that which is without either beginning or end**: [[Rom.16.26|Rom.16:26]], [[Heb.9.14|Heb.9:14]];
(b) **of that which is without beginning**: [[Rom.16.25|Rom.16:25]], [[2Ti.1.9|2Ti.1:9]], [[Tit.1.2|Tit.1:2]];
(with) **of that which is without end **(MM, _VGT_, see word): σκηναί, [[Luk.16.9|Luk.16:9]] οἰκία, [[2Co.5.1|2Co.5:1]] διαθήκη, [[Heb.13.20|Heb.13:20]] εὐαγγέλιον, [[Rev.14.6|Rev.14:6]] παράκλησις, [[2Th.2.16|2Th.2:16]] λύτρωσις, [[Heb.9.12|Heb.9:12]] κληρονομία, ib. 15; κόλασις, [[Mat.25.46|Mat.25:46]] κρίμα, [[Heb.6.2|Heb.6:2]] κρίσις, [[Mrk.3.29|Mrk.3:29]] ὄλεθρον, [[2Th.1.9|2Th.1:9]] πῦρ, [[Mat.18.8|Mat.18:8]] frequently with ζωή, which see
_SYN._: ἀΐδιος, which see (AS)
